int</h2><table><tr><th>#</th><th>Concept</th></tr></table><h3>Key Points</h3><table><tr><th>Point</th></tr><tr><td>Application of Value of a Function at a Point</td></tr><tr><td>Connection of Value of a Function at a Point to other topics</td></tr></table><h3>Common Confusions</h3><table><tr><th>❌ / ✅</th></tr></table><p><b>Summary:</b> Value of a Function at a Point covers essential principles and applications.</p><hr><h2>Right Hand Limit</h2><table><tr><th>#</th><th>Concept</th></tr></table><h3>Key Points</h3><table><tr><th>Point</th></tr><tr><td>Application of Right Hand Limit</td></tr><tr><td>Connection of Right Hand Limit to other topics</td></tr></table><h3>Common Confusions</h3><table><tr><th>❌ / ✅</th></tr></table><p><b>Summary:</b> Right Hand Limit covers essential principles and applications.</p><hr><h2>Left Hand Limit</h2><table><tr><th>#</th><th>Concept</th></tr></table><h3>Key Points</h3><table><tr><th>Point</th></tr><tr><td>Application of Left Hand Limit</td></tr><tr><td>Connection of Left Hand Limit to other topics</td></tr></table><h3>Common Confusions</h3><table><tr><th>❌ / ✅</th></tr></table><p><b>Summary:</b> Left Hand Limit covers essential principles and applications.</p><hr><h2>Existence of Limit (LHL = RHL)</h2><table><tr><th>#</th><th>Concept</th></tr></table><h3>Key Points</h3><table><tr><th>Point</th></tr><tr><td>Application of Existence of Limit (LHL = RHL)</td></tr><tr><td>Connection of Existence of Limit (LHL = RHL) to other topics</td></tr></table><h3>Common Confusions</h3><table><tr><th>❌ / ✅</th></tr></table><p><b>Summary:</b> Existence of Limit (LHL = RHL) covers essential principles and applications.</p><hr><h2>Standard Limits</h2><table><tr><th>#</th><th>Concept</th></tr></table><h3>Key Points</h3><table><tr><th>Point</th></tr><tr><td>Radians are not optional in the trig limits — in degrees the same limit is π/180, which is why every board question states the unit.</td></tr></table><h3>Common Confusions</h3><table><tr><th>❌ / ✅</th